  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1231 PM MDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nA brief isolated thunderstorm over the lowlands cannot be ruled out \nthis afternoon from the better easterly surface flow moving into our \narea with a lingering W-E trough and enhanced diurnal heating. The \nrest of this week should stay dry with seasonal temps thanks to an \nupper ridge developing over the area. This ridge shifts eastward as \na deepening trough moves out of the northeast which increases \nmoisture levels going into the weekend.\n\nPops really take off late Saturday evening over the western half of \nthe CWA but the greatest PWs remain to the east as moisture gets \npulled ahead of the tropical system. This trend remains into early \nnext week where we're seeing the GFS shift most of the incoming \nmoisture from TS Simon to our east with the accompanying low \npressure system to our northwest moving its moisture north of us. \nThe ensembles still show the Rio Grande Valley as the primary area \nof impact from rainfall totals which will bring a risk of flash \nflooding.\n\nWe continue to monitor the path of TS Simon, but it's been trending \nconsistently east of our area. This excess moisture content will \nkeep temperatures below normal through the remainder of the\nperiod.",
